ked hits log as `taken, landed`. Tell me if a stray 0 still shows. |\n| <span class=\"st st-done\">done</span> | **Skill XP saved per adventurer** | 0.1.30 (`5ffe5f3`): `skills_<character>.json` per adventurer, seeded once from the old shared `skills.json` (kept); character select shows the hovered adventurer's levels and combat level; temp-file writes. 0.1.33 added the `skills-saved` check (the save reads back as written); passed in 0.1.35 (test `a4d9016b`). |\n| <span class=\"st st-done\">done</span> | **Prayers block their own style** | Test-mode tally (every hit on the adventurer by attacker, style, prayer and outcome): 0.1.26 to 0.1.28. Protect from Melee blocked chickens, giant rats, goblins and cows; Protect from Missiles blocked Lumbridge guards; Protect from Magic blocked giant frogs (0.1.27, test `401ff9c6`); the wrong prayer let hits through; every enemy hit carried its enemy (only fall damage had none). |\n| <span class=\"st st-doing\">doing</span> | **OSRS music in Bonkscape** | `206af63` (0.1.29), from the `music-research` session: the map's track at stage start (Harmony for Lumbridge) through `OsrsAudio`, Megabonk's music paused, settings `Audio.OsrsMusic` and `Audio.OsrsMusicVolume`. Builds clean, `bonk unstripped` clean, and every type loads without `OsrsKit.Music.dll` (checked offline), so release builds fall back to Megabonk's music. **Heard in game** (2026-10-21) on a local run the user approved, by the `music-research` session: a clean build of 0.2.6 (`2bfc67a`) plus `OsrsKit.Music.dll`, the loader switched on for that run only, then everything restored and checked by sha256. The log: *OSRS music: loading \"Harmony\" (group 76)* at the Lumbridge run's start, then *playing Harmony*, at -24 to -29 dBFS (gain 1.00), with no errors or warnings. Melty test runs (no DLL) keep Megabonk's music. The engine (`OsrsKit.Music.dll`) never goes in the release zip: the publishing gate in `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`; a player-import step comes before any published build can play it. |\n| <span class=\"st st-todo\">todo</span> | **OSRS music for players** | The user asked for the most seamless option (2026-10-21). Most seamless is the engine inside the mod, so players get music with no extra step; that needs either a license from runetunes' author (D0ntPanic; runetunes has no license, see `osrs-kit/src/OsrsKit.Music/PROVENANCE.md`) or an engine of Bonkscape's own written from the documented format (`osrs-kit/docs/research/music-synth.md`) rather than from runetunes' code. An import step on the player's PC (downloading and building runetunes there) would need the Rust toolchain: far from seamless. Suggested: ask the author first (the user sends it; a draft can be prepared), and write Bonkscape's own engine if the answer is no. Until then releases keep Megabonk's music. Decided (the milestone plan, 14bd719): a clean OSRS music engine of our own in osrs-kit, written in a fresh session under clean-room rules (it never reads runetunes' code), in parallel with the releases; whether it ships is a 1.0 decision. |\n| <span class=\"st st-doing\">doing</span> | **Shared osrs-kit** | the osrs-kit repo beside this one (`../osrs-kit`): shared RuneScape code, data dumps and docs. It replaces Bonkscape's own copy of the cache library (src/Bonkscape.Cache, removed by 0.15's switch). Now also holds the music engine (the `OsrsKit.Music` project and its `osrsmusic` tool) and the 13 RuneStar repos with their release files (`reference/runestar`, listed in `data/MANIFEST.md`). Separate session. |\n| <span class=\"st st-doing\">doing</span> | **Map ideas and per-map music choices** | An Ideas layer in `tools/sketch` and `docs/design/`. |\n| <span class=\"st st-done\">done</span> | **Crash at start (0.1.17 to 0.1.21)** | Fixed in 0.1.22 (`d14cd39`). `GUI.DrawTextureWithTexCoords` is stripped from Megabonk's build; Il2CppInterop's rebuilt copy smashed the stack on the first HUD frame of every run (the XP counter's tiled background). Found with test-mode 