d mage as minibosses. The four generals are a boss pool: one is picked as the stage starts, and the portal goes straight to his room, Zilyana's on level 0. There he fights with his three bodyguards, scaled like the 0.10 knights, and his OSRS attacks: K'ril's Prayer smash pierces protection prayers and drains prayer (`pierce_prayer`). No kill-count door: Megabonk's portal can be opened at any time, and a 40-kill gate would need its own panel (the UI pass's work) and a way past it for two-minute tests. Megabonk's Ent3 hovers metres above the model's feet, so at first no general reached melee: Zilyana never attacked. A boss's reach is now measured across the floor. Local: `god-wars`, the four `gwd-*` scenarios and `gwd-kril-melee` pass, each general in his room with his melee and K'ril's Prayer smash landing. A rerun with God Wars second showed the load-time build of every map left out the level (God Wars as level 0's empty box, the adventurer falling through), fixed before the release. Melty test `4f4ef19f` of 0.11.0 passed (graduates; 3 runs): Morytania with Ahrim as the hidden brother (run 1), Ardougne with the knights and Sir Lancelot at Camelot (run 2), and the God Wars Dungeon: the cavern's armies, the portal, then General Graardor in his room with his bodyguards, his melee reaching the adventurer (run 3). |\n\n## Milestone 0.12: the UI pass\n\nEvery screen OSRS-styled with nothing overlapping, doubled or dead, from an OSRS login-style title screen (`docs/design/milestones.md`, 0.12).\n\n| Status | Task | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| <span class=\"st st-done\">done</span> | **Every HUD element at every resolution** | In game at 960x600 and 2560x1600 (0.1.22-0.1.36); `bonk uisprites mock 1280 720 / 1920 1080 / 3840 2160` lays every element out right at 1x, 2x and 4x. Still to see in game: which way the compass turns (`Hud.NorthYaw`) and Megabonk's HUD coming back after a run (`Megabonk HUD restored`). 0.12: Megabonk's HUD comes back after a run (`Megabonk HUD restore