ness | 16 | King Black Dragon | boss | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| ardougne_seers | 0 | Monkey, Goblin, Snake, Giant bat, Guard, Grizzly bear, Guard dog | start | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| ardougne_seers | 1.5 | Warrior, Knight of Ardougne | unlock | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| ardougne_seers | 2 | Warrior, Paladin | miniboss | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| ardougne_seers | 3 | Ogre | unlock | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| ardougne_seers | 3 | Goblin | swarm | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| ardougne_seers | 6 | Guard | swarm | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| ardougne_seers | 7 | Paladin, Hero | miniboss | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| ardougne_seers | 9 | Sir Lancelot | boss | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| god_wars | 0 | Imp, Goblin, Hobgoblin, Aviansie, Bloodveld, Werewolf, Ork | start | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| god_wars | 1.5 | Knight of Saradomin, Saradomin priest | unlock | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| god_wars | 1.5 | Spiritual warrior, Spiritual mage | miniboss | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| god_wars | 2.5 | Goblin | swarm | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| god_wars | 3 | Spiritual ranger | unlock | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| god_wars | 4 | Bloodveld | swarm | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| god_wars | 5 | Spiritual mage, Spiritual warrior | miniboss | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| god_wars | 8 | General Graardor, Kree'arra, K'ril Tsutsaroth, Commander Zilyana | boss | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n<!-- /gen:waves -->\n\nHow those rows apply, each on its own map's stage (Lumbridge on the Forest's first, Ardougne & Seers' Village on its second, the God Wars Dungeon on its third; Al Kharid, Morytania and TzHaar\nCity on the Desert's first, second and third; the Wilderness on the Graveyard's first):\n\n- **start** (minute 0): the run's first monsters. Lumbridge: chickens, goblins, giant rats and guards. Ardougne & Seers' Village: monkeys,\n  goblins, snakes, giant bats, guards, grizzly bears and guard dogs. The God Wars Dungeon: imps, goblins, hobgoblins, aviansies, bloodvelds,\n  werewolves and orks. Al Kharid: scorpions, Shantay Guards,\n  desert lizards, desert wolves, hill giants and Al Kharid warriors. Morytania: Myre\n  blamish snails, bats, crawling hands, ghouls, Loar Shades and banshees. TzHaar City: TzHaar-Hur and TzHaar-Mej. The Wilderness:\n  revenant imps, goblins, hobgoblins and hellhounds, and green dragons.\n- **unlock**: the rows join the spawn pool from that minute. Lumbridge: cows and giant frogs at 1.5. Ardougne & Seers' Village:\n  warriors and Knights of Ardougne at 1.5, ogres at 3. The God Wars Dungeon: Knights of Saradomin and Saradomin priests\n  at 1.5, spiritual rangers at 3. Al Kharid: Kalphite\n  Workers at 1.5, ugthanki and bandits at 3, Kalphite Soldiers at 6. Morytania:\n  vampyre juveniles at 1.5, vampyre juvinates and feral vampyres at 3, the Vyrewatch at 6. TzHaar City:\n  TzHaar-Xil at 1.5, TzHaar-Ket at 3. The Wilderness: revenant demons at 1.5, cyclopes at 3, knights at 7, dragons\n  at 12.\n- **swarm**: Megabonk's swarm event at that minute spawns the row's monsters. Lumbridge: goblins at 4, giant rats at\n  7. Ardougne & Seers' Village: goblins at 3, guards at 6. The God Wars Dungeon: goblins\n  at 2.5, bloodvelds at 4. Al Kharid: scorpions at 4, desert lizards at 7. Morytania: Myre blamish snails at 3,\n  crawling hands at 6. TzHaar City: TzHaar-Hur at 2.5 and 4. The Wilderness: revenant goblins at 4, cyclopes at 8,\n  knights at 11, dragons at 14.\n- **miniboss**: Megabonk's miniboss event at that minute spawns each row's miniboss. Lumbridge: a Cow and a Giant frog\n  at 3 and 8. Ardougne & Seers' Village: a Warrior and a Paladin at 2, a Paladin and a Hero at 7. The God Wars Dungeon: a\n  spiritual warrior and a spiritual mage at 1.5 and 5. Al Kharid:\n  a Kalphite Guardian at 3 and 8. Morytania: Barrows brothers at 2\n  and 7, the five not hidden this run in turn ([below](#the-barrows-brothers)). TzHaar City: a TzHaar-Ket champion at\n  1.5 and 5. The Wilderness: the Chaos Elemental and the Revenant maledictus at 3, 7, 10 and 13.\n- **boss** (minute 10; Ardougne & Seers' Village's and Morytania's 9, the God Wars Dungeon's 8, TzHaar City's 8, the Wilderness's 16): the plan only. The stage boss comes when you open the boss\n  portal (Lumbridge: the Giant Mole; Ardougne & Seers' Village: Sir Lancelot, after the Knights of the\n  Round Table; the God Wars Dungeon: its final portal, this run's general; Al Kharid: the Kalphite Queen; Morytania: the run's hidden Barrows brother); TzHaar City's when you open its final portal\n  (TzTok-Jad, in the Fight Caves), and the Wilderness's when you open its boss door (the King Black Dragon).\n\nA swarm or miniboss row whose minute has no matching event in Megabonk's timeline spawns nothing; the log says how\nmany events each map set (*\"waves: Morytania on Megabonk's Desert stage 1: N timeline events set\"*). Megabonk's own\npacing decides how many monsters spawn and how fast.\n\n## Stand-ins\n\nThe six Barrows brothers are built from their armour (each one's helm, body, legs and weapon); when those items aren't\nin your cache, they use their NPC model and its stand-ins as below.\n\nYour OSRS client downloads a model the first time it shows it, so your cache may not have every monster. For each\nmonster Bonkscape tries its own NPC first, then each **stand-in NPC id** in the order listed, and uses the first one\nwhose models are all in your cache (the log says *\"Goblin: NPC 3031 isn't in this cache, using stand-in NPC 3029\"*).\nIf none is there, the monster borrows the map's fallback monster (Lumbridge, Ardougne & Seers' Village and the God Wars Dungeon: the Goblin; Al Kharid: the Scorpion; Morytania: the Ghoul;\nTzHaar City and its Fight Caves: TzHaar-Hur; the Wilderness: the revenant goblin). If that's missing too, you see\nMegabonk's own model.\n\nTurn stand-ins off with `OSRS.UseStandIns = false` ([Settings](settings.md)).\n\n## Size\n\nA monster's height is worked out when it spawns, and once more a moment later:\n\n1. **OSRS proportions on your adventurer's scale**: its model height in OSRS units, converted to metres exactly like\n   your adventurer's. So an OSRS human (a guard) stands about as tall as your adventurer, and every other monster keeps\n   its OSRS ratio to them.\n2. Times the row's **Size x** (Cow 1.1, Giant frog 1.6, Giant Mole 2.2, the Barrows brothers 1.6, Kalphite Guardian 1.2, Hero and Paladin 1.2, spiritual warrior and mage 1.2, TzHaar-Ket champion 1.2, Chaos Elemental and Revenant\n   maledictus 1.2) and\n   `Models.MonsterSize`.\n3. Times part of Megabonk's own enlargement of elites, minibosses and bosses, capped by tier (below). Megabonk\n   enlarges them a moment after they spawn, so this is applied again once the monster's hitbox is live.\n4. Optionally, at least a share of its Megabonk hitbox's height (`Models.MinHitboxShare`). **Off by default**:\n   Megabonk's hitboxes are tall capsules (5.4 m for a 3 m skeleton), and drawing monsters to fit them undoes the OSRS\n   proportions.\n5. Never taller than its tier's ceiling, measured against your adventurer.\n\n| Tier | Megabonk enlargement passed on, at most | Tallest, as a multiple of your adventurer |\n|---|---|---|\n| Normal | 1.15 x | 1.1 x |\n| Elite | 1.4 x | 1.35 x |\n| Miniboss | 1.6 x | 1.7 x |\n| Boss | 2.0 x | 2.2 x (`Models.BossMaxHeight`) |\n\nModel heights in OSRS units, before step 2, as the main session measured them from the cache (the standing model with\nthe NPC definition's width and height scale): Warrior 216, Guard 201, Cow 153, Giant Mole 150, Goblin 129 (0.64 of a\nguard), Giant rat 125, Giant frog 85, Chicken 79. How big they look next to each other in a run is\n*(unconfirmed: needs a Melty run or footage)*.\n\nA monster's **hitbox** is always Megabonk's; only the drawing changes, so a monster can be hit (and hit you) a little\noutside its drawn shape.\n\n## Animations\n\nEach monster plays its own OSRS sequences (their ids are in the enemies sheet's `animation_ids`):\n\n- **Standing** while it's still.\n- **Walking** while it moves, the cycle sped up or slowed (0.5 to 2.5 times) to match how fast it really goes,\n  against OSRS's one tile per 0.6 s at its size.\n- **Attacking** when it gets within reach of your adventurer (max(1.2 m, 0.4 x its height) + 0.8 m), when a\n  shooter (guards, banshees) starts its ranged or magic attack, and when its hit on you lands; merged with walking\n  when it's still moving and the sequence allows it (as the OSRS client does). An attack plays out (up to 1.4 s)\n  before the next can start.\n- **Dying** where it fell: its body plays the death sequence for up to 1.8 s while Megabonk reuses the enemy.\n\nA monster shown as a [stand-in](#stand-ins) or as the fallback Goblin plays that model's sequences. How the animations\nlook in a run is *(unconfirmed: needs a Melty run or footage)*.\n\n## How monsters move\n\nIn Megabonk, enemies run straight at you. On Bonkscape's maps they find their way on the **OSRS tile grid**\ninstead, like OSRS monsters:\n\n- Every half second, or whenever you step onto a new tile, Bonkscape works out how many steps every tile is from you,\n  moving in 8 directions, never through a wall edge, water or big scenery. A diagonal step needs both side steps open,\n  as in OSRS.\n- Each monster heads for its neighbouring tile that is one step closer, so they go around buildings and over bridges.\n- The search reaches 48 tiles from you in each direction (Morytania's grid is 384 x 450 tiles). Farther out, within\n  3 steps of you, or off the grid, Megabonk's own chase takes over.\n\n## The Giant Mole\n\n<!-- gen:bosses -->\n| Boss | Attacks | Phase thresholds | Pet (rate) | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Giant Mole** | Claw (melee, 0 ms telegraph, contact); Dig (melee, 1200 ms telegraph, burrow teleport every 12s) | 50% HP | Baby Mole, 1/50 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **TzTok-Jad** | Magic (magic, 1800 ms telegraph, random); Ranged (ranged, 1800 ms telegraph, random); Bite (melee, 0 ms telegraph, random) | 50% HP | TzRek-Jad, 1/20 | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Kalphite Queen** | Jaws (melee, 0 ms telegraph, random); Spines (ranged, 600 ms telegraph, random); Lightning (magic, 900 ms telegraph, random) | 50% HP | Kalphite Princess, 1/50 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **King Black Dragon** | Bite (melee, 0 ms telegraph, random); Dragonfire (magic, 600 ms telegraph, random); Toxic breath (magic, 600 ms telegraph, random); Icy breath (magic, 600 ms telegraph, random); Shocking breath (magic, 600 ms telegraph, random) | 50% HP | Prince Black Dragon, 1/30 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Sir Lancelot** | Slash (melee, 0 ms telegraph, random); Lunge (melee, 0 ms telegraph, random) | 50% HP | - | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **General Graardor** | Smash (melee, 0 ms telegraph, random); Slam (ranged, 600 ms telegraph, random) | 50% HP | Pet General Graardor, 1/40 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Kree'arra** | Wind (ranged, 600 ms telegraph, random); Tornado (magic, 600 ms telegraph, random); Claw (melee, 0 ms telegraph, random) | 50% HP | Pet Kree'arra, 1/40 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **K'ril Tsutsaroth** | Slash (melee, 0 ms telegraph, random); Prayer smash (melee, 0 ms telegraph, random); Fireball (magic, 600 ms telegraph, random) | 50% HP | Pet K'ril Tsutsaroth, 1/40 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Commander Zilyana** | Sword (melee, 0 ms telegraph, random); Light (magic, 0 ms telegraph, random) | 50% HP | Pet Zilyana, 1/40 | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n<!-- /gen:bosses -->\n\nThe Giant Mole is Lumbridge's stage boss <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span>. You call it by using the boss portal\nat the swamp's dark hole ([Maps](maps.md)). **The fight then moves into the Mole's lair** (0.2.10): the screen shows\n*Loading - please wait.* for a moment, and you land in the Falador Mole Lair from your own OSRS cache, with the Mole\nin the middle of it and the chat box saying *\"You follow the Giant Mole down into its lair.\"* The cave is darker, with\nblack beyond its walls. Monsters still alive come with you, and chests and shrines move onto the lair's open ground.\n\nThe Mole attacks with Megabonk's own boss attacks; Protect from Melee halves them, its ground attacks too (a hit\nthat names no monster counts as the nearest boss's within 30 m). Bonkscape adds its **dig**:\n\n1. **12 seconds** after it appears, and 12 seconds after each dig, the chat box says *\"The Giant Mole burrows into\n   the ground!\"* and it plays its OSRS burrowing sequence (3314). Without the sequences in your cache, it sinks into\n   the ground over 1.2 s instead.\n2. Once it's under, it moves: **in its lair, to another spot 8 to 18 steps' walk from you** (never behind a wall you\n   can't get round), as in OSRS. If the lair couldn't be built, the fight stays on the map and it surfaces next to you.\n3. It comes back up with its OSRS surfacing sequence (3315), or rises over 1.2 s.\n\nBelow **50% HP** it digs more often, every 8 seconds. After the kill you stay in the lair. Where Megabonk's portal\nto the next stage appears then is *(unconfirmed: needs a Melty run or footage)*: no test run has killed the Mole yet.\nDying in the lair restarts the run on Lumbridge with its own sky.\n\nIts death can drop its pet, the Baby mole (1 in 50, [Boss pets](#boss-pets)). Planned for the Mole: its own drop (the\nMole claw) and OSRS stats; neither is built.\n\n## Ardougne and Seers' Village\n\nArdougne & Seers' Village's monsters are its townsfolk and wildlife, all melee but the guards (ranged): monkeys,\ngoblins, snakes, giant bats, guards, grizzly bears and guard dogs from the start, warriors and Knights of Ardougne\nfrom 1.5 minutes, ogres from 3. Its minibosses are **Heroes** and **Paladins** (size x 1.2), with Megabonk's miniboss\nstats and attacks. Its boss is Sir Lancelot, after the other Knights of the Round Table.\n\n## The Knights of the Round Table\n\nOpening the boss portal at Camelot doesn't move the fight: the knights come to you on the map, in waves, while Sir\nLancelot (OSRS NPC 4354, on Megabonk's `Ent2`) waits where he rose, unseen, frozen and unhurt:\n\n| Time | Knights |\n|---|---|\n| 0 s | Sir Bedivere and Sir Pelleas |\n| 15 s | Sir Tristram and Sir Palomedes |\n| 30 s | Sir Lucan, Sir Gawain and Sir Kay |\n| 45 s, or once every knight is down | Sir Lancelot: *\"Sir Lancelot appears!\"* |\n\nEach knight has his own row's HP (196 to 239, scaled like the map's monsters) and speed, and fights with the attacks of the Megabonk enemy he rides.\nSir Lancelot's attacks are OSRS's: every **2.4 seconds**, start to start, a Slash or a Lunge (melee, only when you're\nbeside him), each dealt as 13% to 20% of your maximum health (his max hit, 23, against Jad's 97). Megabonk's own\nattacks for `Ent2` are off and touching him doesn't hurt. Protect from Melee halves his hits, as for any boss. His\nHP is Megabonk's boss's.\n\n## The God Wars Dungeon\n\nThe God Wars Dungeon's monsters are the four gods' armies: imps, goblins, hobgoblins, aviansies, bloodvelds, werewolves\nand orks from the start, Knights of Saradomin and Saradomin priests from 1.5 minutes, spiritual rangers from 3. Its\nminibosses are **spiritual warriors** and **spiritual mages** (size x 1.2), with Megabonk's miniboss stats and\nattacks. Its boss is one of the four generals.\n\n## The God Wars generals\n\nEach run one general is picked at random to be the God Wars Dungeon's final boss: opening the final portal loads\nMegabonk's final stage, and the fight moves into his room ([Maps](maps.md#the-generals-rooms)), where he comes at once\nwith his three bodyguards: *\"You enter General Graardor's arena; the waves come first.\"* Each general rides\nMegabonk's `Ent3`, with Megabonk's boss HP; his bodyguards fight with the attacks of the Megabonk enemies they ride.\nMegabonk's own attacks for `Ent3` are off and touching a general doesn't hurt: his attacks are OSRS's, picked by\nweight, start to start, and a melee one only when you're beside him (measured across the floor):\n\n| General | Bodyguards | Every | Attacks (weight; hit as a share of your maximum health) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **General Graardor** (Bandos) | Sergeants Strongstack, Steelwill and Grimspike | 3.6 s | Smash, melee (2; 34% to 53%); Slam, ranged, lands 1.8 s after (1; 20% to 31%) |\n| **Kree'arra** (Armadyl) | Flight Kilisa, Wingman Skree, Flockleader Geerin | 1.8 s | Wind, ranged, 1.8 s (2; 39% to 60%); Tornado, magic, 1.8 s (1; 12% to 18%); Claw, melee (0.5; 15% to 23%) |\n| **K'ril Tsutsaroth** (Zamorak) | Tstanon Karlak, Zakl'n Gritch, Balfrug Kreeyath | 3.6 s | Slash, melee (8; 26% to 40%; a quarter of the time it poisons you for 5 s); Prayer smash, melee (4; 28% to 43%); Fireball, magic, 1.8 s (6; 17% to 26%) |\n| **Commander Zilyana** (Saradomin) | Starlight, Growler, Bree | 1.2 s | Sword, melee (1; 15% to 24%); Light, magic, beside her only, 0.6 s (1; 11% to 18%) |\n\nThe hits are scaled by each attack's OSRS max hit against Jad's 97. The right protection prayer halves them, as for\nany boss, and stops K'ril's poison, except his **Prayer smash**: it goes straight through your protection prayer and\ndrains your prayer points, half your maximum times the share of your health it took.\n\nThe general's death ends the run, and can drop his pet (1 in 40, [Boss pets](#boss-pets)). Melty's test of 0.11.0 showed General\nGraardor in his room with his bodyguards, his melee reaching the adventurer; the other generals, the Prayer smash and\na general's death are *(unconfirmed: needs a Melty run or footage)*\n\n## Al Kharid\n\nAl Kharid's monsters are desert folk and beasts, all melee: scorpions, Shantay Guards, desert lizards, desert wolves,\nhill giants and Al Kharid warriors from the start, Kalphite Workers from 1.5 minutes, ugthanki and bandits from 3,\nKalphite Soldiers from 6. Its minibosses are **Kalphite Guardians** (OSRS NPC 960, on Megabonk's `MinibossScorpion`\nand `MinibossGolemSand`, size x 1.2), with Megabonk's miniboss stats and attacks. Its boss is the Kalphite Queen.\n\n## The Kalphite Queen\n\nOpening Al Kharid's boss portal moves the fight into [the Kalphite Lair](maps.md#the-kalphite-lair). The Queen (OSRS\nNPC 963, on Megabonk's `Pharaoh1`) fights in two forms, as in OSRS: **crawling** first, then **airborne**.\n\n**Her attacks are OSRS's.** Megabonk's own attacks are off and touching her doesn't hurt. Every **2.4 seconds**, start\nto start, she uses one of three at random, with her form's OSRS animation and graphics:\n\n| Attack | Style | Lands | |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Jaws | melee | 0.3 s after she starts it | Only when you're beside her; it misses if you've stepped away |\n| Spines | ranged | 1.8 s after | Her spines fly at you |\n| Lightning | magic | 2.1 s after | Lightning strikes you |\n\nHer OSRS max hit is 31 against Jad's 97, so a hit is dealt as 18% to 27% of your maximum health. The right protection\nprayer halves it, as for any boss (only Jad's are blocked completely).\n\n**Her second form.** When the crawling Queen dies, her death is called off: she's back at full health, the crawling\nhusk stays behind, and she rises airborne (OSRS NPC 965), still and unhurt while she rises; the chat says *\"Kalphite\nQueen rises again!\"* Then she fights on with the same attacks in her airborne animations. Only her second death\ncounts: it ends the fight and the stage. *(unconfirmed: needs a Melty run or footage)*\n\nHer second death can drop her pet, the Kalphite princess (1 in 50, [Boss pets](#boss-pets)).\n\n## The Wilderness\n\nThe Wilderness's monsters are revenants, from imps to dragons, and green dragons, all melee. Its minibosses are the\n**Chaos Elemental** (magic) and the **Revenant maledictus** (ranged), size x 1.2, with Megabonk's miniboss stats and\nattacks. Its boss is the King Black Dragon.\n\n**PKers.** Six player killers in classic gear hunt you there, never part of the waves: one ambushes you 60 to\n90 seconds into the stage, then one every three to four minutes, from 8 to 14 tiles away, with *\"Ice Tank is attacking\nyou!\"* (its name). None comes while you're in a boss's lair.\n\n| PKer | Combat | Weapon and special attack |\n|---|---|---|\n| Pure Spec | 70 | Magic shortbow (Snapshot) |\n| Ice Tank | 98 | Ice Barrage (Deep Freeze) |\n| Pipe Ranger | 104 | Toxic blowpipe (Toxic Siphon) |\n| Whip Hybrid | 112 | Abyssal whip (Energy Drain) |\n| Ags Main | 126 | Armadyl godsword (The Judgement) |\n| Claw Swap | 126 | Dragon claws (Slice and Dice) |\n\nEach is an OSRS player body in its gear, with HP set by its combat level; its ordinary hits are those of the\nMegabonk monster it stands in for. Every 10 to 14 seconds, when\nyou're in its reach (4.5 m for melee, 18 m otherwise), it fires its weapon's special attack, with its OSRS animation\nand graphic: a hit of 20% to 33% of your maximum health, which the protection prayer for its style cuts as for any\nmonster.\n\n## The King Black Dragon\n\nThe Graveyard's final boss, in [his lair](maps.md#the-king-black-dragons-lair) below the boss door: OSRS NPC 239, on\nMegabonk's `Ent1`. His HP is Megabonk's final boss's. Megabonk's own attacks are off and touching him doesn't hurt;\nevery **2.4 seconds**, start to start, he picks one of five OSRS attacks by weight:\n\n| Attack | Style | Lands | Weight | Hit, as a share of your maximum health |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Bite | melee | 0.3 s after he starts it; only beside him | 1.5 | 14% to 22% |\n| Dragonfire | magic | 1.8 s after | 1.5 | 37% to 57% |\n| Toxic breath | magic | 1.8 s after | 0.5 | 28% to 44%; half the time it poisons you for 5 s |\n| Icy breath | magic | 1.8 s after | 0.5 | 28% to 44%; half the time it freezes you in place for 3 s |\n| Shocking breath | magic | 1.8 s after | 0.5 | 28% to 44%; half the time it slows you for 3 s |\n\nSo beside him a third of his attacks are bites, and away from him half are dragonfire. The hits are scaled by his OSRS\nmax hits (25, 65 and 50) against Jad's 97. **Protect from Magic** halves his fire and breaths, as for any boss, and\nstops the breaths' poison, freeze and shock. In OSRS an anti-dragon shield blocks dragonfire; there's none here.\n\nHis death ends the run, and can drop his pet, the Prince black dragon (1 in 30, [Boss pets](#boss-pets)). The breaths' effects and his death\nare *(unconfirmed: needs a Melty run or footage)*\n\n## The Barrows brothers\n\nMorytania's boss is one of the six Barrows brothers, **hidden**: each time Morytania's stage starts, one is picked at\nrandom, and he rises when you open the boss portal at the Barrows\n([Maps](maps.md#morytania)), named on the boss bar. The other five are the map's **minibosses**, one after another at\nMegabonk's miniboss events. All six take over Megabonk's `Pharaoh2` (as the boss) and its `MinibossGolemSand` and\n`MinibossScorpion` (as minibosses), size x 1.6, each in his own armour with his own weapon and animations. As boss or\nminiboss they keep Megabonk's attacks and stats.\n\n| Brother | Style | Set effect, on his hits (and yours, when you play him) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Dharok the Wretched** | melee | Every hit grows as the hitter's health drops, up to +98% at 1 hitpoint |\n| **Ahrim the Blighted** | magic | 25% of magic hits: whoever was hit hits 10% weaker for 6 s |\n| **Guthan the Infested** | melee | 25% of melee hits: the hitter heals by the damage dealt |\n| **Karil the Tainted** | ranged | 25% of ranged hits: whoever was hit is slowed for 4 s (a monster to 80% speed) |\n| **Torag the Corrupted** | melee | 25% of melee hits: whoever was hit is slowed for 2 s (a monster to 80% speed); OSRS drains run energy, which Megabonk doesn't have |\n| **Verac the Defiled** | melee | 25% of melee hits: his hit on you ignores your protection prayer; your hit on a monster does 25% more |\n\nA brother's set works on his projectiles and slams too: a hit on you that names no monster counts as the nearest\nbrother's within 10 m. Each effect but Dharok's plays its OSRS graphic.\n\n**The Barrows chest.** Beating the hidden brother gives, besides Megabonk's own reward, one **Barrows piece** you don't\nown yet, picked at random from all 24 (each brother's helm, body, legs and weapon): *\"You find Dharok's helm in the\nBarrows chest!\"* Pieces are yours for good, shared by all your adventurers. A brother's four pieces together unlock him\nas an [adventurer](adventurers.md#unlocking): *\"You have Dharok's full set: he can join you as an adventurer.\"* With\nall 24 owned, the chest gives nothing more.\n\nMelty's test of 0.7.0 showed Torag the Corrupted as the hidden boss, named on the boss bar and swinging his hammers.\nThe set effects, the chest's pieces and a brother's unlock are *(unconfirmed: needs a Melty run or footage)*\n\n## TzHaar City\n\nTzHaar City's monsters are the TzHaar, on the Desert's enemy types from its third stage on: **TzHaar-Hur** and\n**TzHaar-Mej** (magic) from the start, **TzHaar-Xil** from 1.5 minutes and **TzHaar-Ket** from 3. Its minibosses are\n**TzHaar-Ket champions** (OSRS NPC 7679, on Megabonk's `MinibossScorpion` and `MinibossGolemSand`, size x 1.2): as\nminibosses they keep Megabonk's stats and attacks, and a protection prayer halves their hits. Its boss is TzTok-Jad,\nin the Fight Caves.\n\n## TzTok-Jad\n\nOpening TzHaar City's final portal moves the fight into the [Fight Caves](maps.md#the-fight-caves), as the Mole's\nportal moves it into its lair. TzTok-Jad (OSRS NPC 3127, on Megabonk's `Pharaoh3`) is placed on his tile there but\nheld out of the fight, unseen, frozen and unhurt, while six waves of Fight Caves monsters come first, each 6 to 16\ntiles from you on ground you can reach:\n\n| Time in the caves | What comes |\n|---|---|\n| 0 s | 6 Tz-Kih |\n| 20 s | 6 Tz-Kek |\n| 40 s | 6 Tok-Xil (ranged) |\n| 60 s | 6 Yt-MejKot |\n| 80 s | 3 Ket-Zek (magic) |\n| 100 s | 6 Ket-Zek |\n| 120 s | TzTok-Jad: *\"TzTok-Jad appears!\"* |\n\nThe waves are timed: each comes whether or not the last is dead. Their monsters are OSRS models on Megabonk's enemy\ntypes and fight with those types' attacks; their OSRS abilities (Tz-Kek splitting, Yt-MejKot healing, Tok-Xil's\nspines, Ket-Zek's fire) aren't built.\n\n**His attacks are OSRS's, not Megabonk's.** Megabonk's own attacks for `Pharaoh3` are switched off, and touching him\ndoesn't hurt. Two seconds after he appears, and then every 4.8 seconds (start to start, as in OSRS), he starts one of\nthree attacks at random, with its OSRS animation and graphics:\n\n| Attack | Style | Lands | |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Magic | magic | 3.1 s after he starts it | A fireball flies from him to you |\n| Ranged | ranged | 3.1 s after he starts it | A boulder falls on you |\n| Bite | melee | 0.3 s after he starts it | Only when you're beside him; it misses if you've stepped away |\n\nA hit is dealt as 55% to 85% of your maximum health (his Magic attack, whose max hit is 95 to the others' 97, 54% to 83%), through Megabonk's own damage (armour still counts). The protection prayer for its style, on when the hit **lands**, blocks\nit completely ([Prayer](prayer.md#what-it-blocks)): watch his wind-up and switch, as in OSRS.\n\n**Healers.** The first time he drops below half health, the chat box says *\"TzTok-Jad calls for help!\"* and four\n**Yt-HurKot** appear around him. They walk to him and, once beside him, heal him 2% of his maximum health every 1.2\nseconds. Hit one and it leaves him for good and comes after you.\n\n**The Fire cape.** Killing him unlocks the [Fire cape](gear-passives.md#the-fire-cape) for the adventurer you're\nplaying: *\"You have been awarded a Fire cape!\"* His death can also drop his pet,\nTzRek-Jad (1 in 20, [Boss pets](#boss-pets)).\n\nAs a boss his HP is Megabonk's (its `Pharaoh3`'s), times TzHaar City's difficulty of 1. Melty's test of 0.5.0 showed\nthe Fight Caves, the waves and Jad joining the fight; his attacks against a prayer, the healers, his death and the\nFire cape are *(unconfirmed: needs a Melty run or footage)*.\n\n## Loot\n\nMonsters drop Megabonk's normal pickups, dressed as OSRS items, plus Bonkscape's own prayer potions:\n\n| Drop | What it is | What it does |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Coins** (in TzHaar City, **Tokkul**) | Megabonk's gold, drawn as the map's OSRS currency stack for the amount (coins: 1 coin up to the big pile) | Megabonk's gold |\n| **Shrimps** (60%), **Lobster** (30%), **Shark** (10%) | Megabonk's health pickup, as a random OSRS food | Heals 15, 30 or 60 HP in place of Megabonk's amount: *\"You eat the shrimps. It heals some health.\"* |\n| **Prayer potion(4)** | Bonkscape's own pickup, 2.5% chance per kill | Restores prayer points ([Prayer](prayer.md#prayer-potions)) |\n| **Casket** | Megabonk's chest | Megabonk's chest reward, and [evolutions](weapons-and-evolutions.md#evolutions) |\n| **Clue scroll (easy)** | Bonkscape's own pickup, 0.2% chance per kill (1 in 500) | Starts a clue trail ([Clue scrolls](#clue-scrolls)) |\n\nThe sheet also plans the Giant Mole's own drop, the Mole claw; it isn't built.\n\n## Boss pets\n\nA boss with an OSRS pet can drop it when its last form dies (the Kalphite Queen's second):\n\n| Boss | Pet | Chance |\n|---|---|---|\n| Giant Mole | Baby mole | 1 in 50 |\n| TzTok-Jad | TzRek-Jad | 1 in 20 |\n| Kalphite Queen | Kalphite princess | 1 in 50 |\n| King Black Dragon | Prince black dragon | 1 in 30 |\n| Each God Wars general | his own pet | 1 in 40 |\n\nSir Lancelot and the Barrows brothers have none. A drop says *\"You have a funny feeling like you're being followed.\"*,\nor *\"You have a funny feeling like you would have been followed...\"* for a pet you already own.\n\nA pet is yours for good, for every adventurer (kept in `unlocks.json`). One is out at a time: your first pet comes out\nat once, and the pet line on character select (*\"Pet: ...\"*, *\"Click to change\"*) goes through the ones you own, then\nnone. The pet out follows you through each run as its OSRS NPC, walking and standing with its own animations, and\ngives every adventurer +1% luck (Megabonk's Luck). *(unconfirmed: needs a Melty run or footage)*\n\n## Clue scrolls\n\nAny kill can drop an **easy clue scroll**, a 0.2% chance (1 in 500), while you have no clue going. It spins on the\nground and slides to you once you're within about 9 m: *\"You find a clue scroll!\"* and *\"You read the clue scroll: 3\nsteps on Lumbridge & Swamp.\"*\n\nThe trail is 2 or 3 of the map's own clue steps, nearest first, each a dig, a search or a talk:\n\n- The step's hint shows in the chat box, as a dialogue (*\"Clue scroll (easy): step 1 of 2\"*) for a few seconds, and\n  stays under the minimap. OSRS's yellow hint arrow stands over the spot, and a minimap arrow marks it (on the\n  minimap's edge when it's further away). For a talk step, the NPC stands at the spot, facing you.\n- Stand there for 0.8 s (within 1.5 tiles to dig, 1.8 to search, 2.5 to talk): *\"You dig and find another clue (2 of\n  3).\"*\n- The last step pays a **reward casket**: 100 to 200 coins (*\"You dig and find a reward casket: 150 coins!\"*) and one\n  of Megabonk's free chests.\n\nOne clue at a time. It waits while you're in a boss's lair, and moving on to another stage loses it.\n\n## Planned monsters\n\nThe Vyrewatch Sentinel is in the roster above as a planned row (phase 2). It doesn't spawn. Nor does the small Tz-Kek\na Tz-Kek splits into in OSRS: its row is there, but the split isn't built.\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/EnemySkins.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Animator.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Bosses.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Pathing.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Content.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Loot.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Combat.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Core/Sizing.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Core/Osrs.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Core/Rows.cs sheets/enemies.json sheets/bosses.json sheets/waves.json sheets/drops.json src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/BossFight.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Bonk.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Unlocks.cs sheets/maps.json src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Barrows.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/SetEffects.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/SecondForm.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Pkers.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Graveyard.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Pets.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Clues.cs sheets/clue_steps.json -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "prayer", "text": "# Prayer\n\nEvery monster fights in one combat style (melee, ranged or magic), shown by the icon over the nearest monsters. A\n**protection prayer** against that style blocks its hits. <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span>\n\n<!-- gen:prayers -->\n| Prayer | Blocks | Normal monsters | Bosses | Drain (points/s) | Default key | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Protect from Melee** | melee | 100% | 50% | 0.333 | 1 | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Protect from Missiles** | ranged | 100% | 50% | 0.333 | 2 | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Protect from Magic** | magic | 100% | 50% | 0.333 | 3 | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n<!-- /gen:prayers -->\n\n## Using prayers\n\n- Press **1**, **2** or **3** to turn on Protect from Melee, Missiles or Magic. Change the keys with `Prayer.Keys`\n  ([Settings](settings.md)). On a controller: d-pad left, up or right (`Controller.Prayers`).\n- **One at a time**: turning one on replaces the one that was on. Press its key again to turn it off.\n- Each prayer plays its OSRS sound when it goes on, and the prayer-off sound when you turn it off.\n- The keys do nothing while you're typing in Megabonk's chat.\n- While a prayer is on, its OSRS **overhead icon** floats above your adventurer.\n\n## What it blocks\n\nWhen a monster hits you and your prayer matches **that monster's style**:\n\n| Monster | Damage blocked |\n|---|---|\n| Bosses (anything Megabonk flags as a boss, stage boss or final boss, such as the Giant Mole) | **50%** |\n| TzTok-Jad's own attacks | **100%**, when the prayer matches the attack's style as it lands ([Monsters](monsters-and-bosses.md#tztok-jad)) |\n| Every other monster | **100%**: the hit shows as a blue 0 hitsplat |\n\nA boss's hit that names no monster (the Giant Mole's ground attacks) counts as the nearest boss's within 30 m, so its\nprotection prayer works on it. Megabonk counts its minibosses as bosses (a test run's log: `MinibossGolem \u2026 IsBoss True`), so a protection prayer\nhalves a miniboss's hits too, like the Giant Mole's. Elites aren't bosses: prayers stop all of their damage.\n\nThe overhead prayer icon glints (a small sparkle) whenever the prayer stops or halves a hit. Hits from a style you're\nnot praying against go through in full. A quarter of Verac the Defiled's melee hits ignore the prayer\n([Barrows brothers](monsters-and-bosses.md#the-barrows-brothers)). K'ril Tsutsaroth's Prayer smash goes through every protection prayer and drains your prayer points\n([Monsters](monsters-and-bosses.md#the-god-wars-generals)). Protect from Magic also stops the King Black Dragon's breaths from poisoning, freezing or shocking you\n([Monsters](monsters-and-bosses.md#the-king-black-dragon)). Lava burns ([Maps](maps.md#tzhaar-city)) have no style, so no prayer stops\nthem. Checked in test runs: Protect from Melee stops chickens, giant rats, goblins\nand cows, Protect from Missiles stops Lumbridge guards, Protect from Magic stops giant frogs, and the wrong prayer\nlets hits through.\n\n## Prayer points\n\n- You start every run with **20 + your Prayer level** points (21 at Prayer 1, 119 at 99).\n- An active prayer drains **0.333 points a second**, one point every 3 seconds.\n- While a prayer is on you earn **2 Prayer XP a second** ([Skills](skills-and-xp.md)), so a higher Prayer level means\n  more points in later runs.\n- At 0 points the prayer switches off with OSRS's empty-prayer sound and the chat says *\"You have run out of Prayer\n  points, you can recharge at an altar.\"* Pressing a key with no points left says *\"You need to recharge your Prayer\n  at an altar.\"* Bonkscape has no altars to pray at yet: potions are the only way back.\n\n## Prayer potions\n\nEach kill has a **2.5%** chance to drop a **Prayer potion(4)**. It spins on the ground, slides towards you once you're\nwithin about 9 m, and you drink it when you get close: **7 points + 25% of your maximum**, *\"You drink some of your\nprayer potion.\"*\n\n## The prayer book\n\nThe side panel's prayer tab, in the lower right (**F5**, `Interface.PrayerTabKey`, or a click on the tab), shows the\nthree protection prayers at their places in OSRS's prayer book, each with its key in the corner. The active one sits\non OSRS's glow and its key turns yellow. When you're out of points, the prayers that aren't on are dimmed. Your points\nshow under the book, as *\"43 / 52\"* ([HUD](hud-and-chat.md#the-side-panel)).\n\nYour prayer points are on the **prayer orb** beside the minimap ([HUD](hud-and-chat.md#in-a-run)): the number is green\nwhen full, yellow at half and red when empty, and the orb lights up while a prayer is on.\n\nFor the first 45 seconds of a run, a hint above the side panel reads *\"Pray against the icon over a monster: 1 Melee  2\nMissiles  3 Magic  (F5: prayers, F1: attack style)\"*.\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Prayer.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Hud.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/HudLayout.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Loot.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Combat.cs sheets/prayers.json sheets/drops.json src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/BossFight.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/LavaBurn.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/SetEffects.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Inventory.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Controls.cs -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "settings", "text": "# Settings\n\nBonkscape's settings are in **`BepInEx/config/gg.melty.bonkscape.cfg`** in Megabonk's folder. BepInEx writes the file,\nwith every key at its default, the first time Megabonk starts with Bonkscape. Edit it with Megabonk closed: settings\nare read once, when the game starts. For every number key but `Audio.OsrsVolume`, a value outside the range is clamped to the nearest end.\n\n| Section | Key | Default | Range | What it does |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `OSRS` | `CacheFolder` | *(empty)* | a folder | The folder holding OSRS's `main_file_cache.dat2` and `.idx` files. Empty: Bonkscape finds it ([Getting started](getting-started.md#where-bonkscape-looks-for-your-osrs-files)). |\n| `OSRS` | `UseStandIns` | `true` | true / false | When a monster's own model isn't in your cache, use the next stand-in NPC that is ([Monsters](monsters-and-bosses.md#stand-ins)). Off: such monsters borrow the Goblin's model, or keep Megabonk's. |\n| `Models` | `AdventurerScale` | `1.6` | 0.5 to 3 | Your adventurer's height as a share of Megabonk's character (1 = the same height). OSRS monsters and the OSRS maps scale with it. |\n| `Models` | `MonsterSize` | `1.0` | 0.3 to 3 | OSRS monsters' size relative to your adventurer's scale. 1 = OSRS proportions: OSRS humans (guards) about as tall as your adventurer, goblins, rats and chickens smaller. An old `MonsterScale` line is ignored. |\n| `Models` | `MinHitboxShare` | `0` | 0 to 2 | Draw monsters at least this share of their Megabonk hitbox's height, up to their size ceiling. 0 = off: Megabonk's hitboxes are tall capsules (5.4 m for a 3 m skeleton), so a floor undoes OSRS proportions. Replaced `HitboxFill` (0.85, then 0.6) in 0.1.15; an old `HitboxFill` line is ignored. |\n| `Models` | `BossMaxHeight` | `2.2` | 1 to 6 | The tallest a boss may be drawn, as a multiple of your adventurer's height. |\n| `Camera` | `Distance` | `0.8` | 0.4 to 1.5 | Megabonk's follow camera distance (1 = Megabonk's own; lower = closer). Scales both the camera's offset (about 11 m) and the extra zoom-out it adds as hordes grow (up to about 15 m). |\n| `Camera` | `FarDistance` | `1.6` | 0.4 to 3 | The far camera distance that `ToggleKey` switches to, on the same scale as `Distance`. |\n| `Camera` | `NearPitch` | `45` | 5 to 85 | Degrees the near camera looks down. Every run starts (and restarts, and enters or leaves a boss's lair) facing north at this pitch, as OSRS's camera does at the Lumbridge respawn; turn it freely after. Megabonk's own pitch is 20. |\n| `Camera` | `FarPitch` | `65` | 5 to 85 | Degrees the far camera looks down when `ToggleKey` picks it: OSRS's highest camera is about 67, almost straight down. |\n| `Camera` | `ToggleKey` | `V` | a Unity key name | Switches the camera between `Distance` (near) and `FarDistance` (far) during a run; the chat says *Camera: far.* or *Camera: near.* A name Unity doesn't know keeps `V`. |\n| `Special` | `FireKey` | `F` | a Unity key name | Fires the armed weapon's special attack at the nearest monster in reach, if the special attack bar has enough energy (each spec's cost is its OSRS one; Bonkscape's invented magic specs cost 50%). Nothing in reach or too little energy spends nothing. |\n| `Special` | `SwitchKey` | `Q` | a Unity key name | Arms the next weapon you hold that has a special attack; the chat names it. |\n| `Minimap` | `Zoom` | `2.5` | 1 to 6 | Zooms Megabonk's minimap in on the OSRS maps (1 = Megabonk's own scale; OSRS's minimap is about 3x closer). |\n| `Map` | `RealLumbridge` | `true` | true / false | Build the real OSRS maps from your cache as the arenas: Lumbridge, Ardougne & Seers' Village and the God Wars Dungeon on the Forest; Al Kharid, Morytania and TzHaar City on the Desert's three stages; the Wilderness on the Graveyard; and the bosses' lairs. Off: Megabonk's stages with OSRS scenery ([Maps](maps.md#when-a-map-isnt-built)). The key keeps its old name so existing settings files still work. |\n| `Map` | `LargeMapMinFaces` | `300` | 0 to 5000 | On large maps (over 40,000 tiles, such as Morytania): leave out ground decorations (flowers, grass tufts, small stones) and small scenery that blocks nothing and has fewer faces than this. 0 keeps every object, which nearly doubles what Morytania has to build and draw. |\n| `Map` | `DrawDistance` | `200` | 0 to 5000 | OSRS scenery and walls farther than this many metres from your adventurer aren't drawn; the ground always is. 0 draws everything. |\n| `Audio` | `OsrsVolume` | `0.55` | 0 to 1 | Volume of OSRS sound effects (0 = silent). Not clamped, so keep it in range. |\n| `Audio` | `OsrsMusic` | `true` | true or false | EXPERIMENTAL: play each map's OSRS track from your cache (Lumbridge: Harmony) instead of Megabonk's music. Needs `OsrsKit.Music.dll`, which release builds don't include, so in a release it does nothing. |\n| `Audio` | `OsrsMusicVolume` | `1` | 0 to 2 | OSRS music volume relative to Megabonk's own music volume setting. |\n| `Interface` | `OsrsWindows` | `true` | true or false | Give Megabonk's windows OSRS's look: its menus, character and map select, settings, the pause menu, level-up offers and shop get OSRS's stone backgrounds, its two-line borders and stone buttons in place of their own (a chest window keeps its teal background: [Known limitations](known-limitations.md)); every button works as before. Off: Megabonk's look. |\n| `Interface` | `TitleScreen` | `true` | true or false | Show OSRS's login screen (its background, logo and login box, from your OSRS cache) in place of Megabonk's main menu. Its buttons run Megabonk's own menu functions: Play, Shop, Unlocks, Quests, Settings, Exit, Leaderboards, Credits, Language, Discord; Enter or Space plays. Off: Megabonk's main menu. |\n| `Interface` | `PrayerTabKey` | `F5` | a Unity key name | Key that switches the side panel (bottom right) between the inventory and the prayer book, as OSRS's F5 does; a click on a tab works too. |\n| `Interface` | `AttackStyleKey` | `F1` | a Unity key name | Key that switches to your next attack style, which decides the skill your hits train (melee: Accurate trains Attack, Aggressive Strength, Defensive Defence, Controlled all three; ranged: Accurate, Rapid, Longrange; magic: casting, defensive casting). It shows the combat tab for a few seconds; a click on the combat tab (the crossed swords) opens it, and a click on a style picks it. Your style is kept per adventurer. F1 is OSRS's own key for the combat tab. |\n| `Prayer` | `Keys` | `Alpha1,Alpha2,Alpha3` | three Unity key names | Keys for Protect from Melee, Missiles and Magic, comma-separated, as Unity `KeyCode` names: `Alpha1` is the 1 key above the letters, `Keypad1` the number pad's, `Z`, `X`, `C` letters. A name Unity doesn't know keeps that prayer's default. |\n| `Controller` | `Prayers` | `DPadLeft,DPadUp,DPadRight` | three button names | Controller buttons for Protect from Melee, Missiles and Magic, comma-separated, as buttons of Rewired's standard gamepad layout so they mean the same on any pad: `A`, `B`, `X`, `Y`, `LeftBumper`, `RightBumper`, `Back`, `Start`, `LeftStickButton`, `RightStickButton`, `DPadUp`, `DPadRight`, `DPadDown`, `DPadLeft`, or `None`. The defaults are buttons Megabonk leaves free in a run. Controller buttons do nothing while a Megabonk window has the game paused (its d-pad moves through the window). A name Bonkscape doesn't know keeps that button's default. The keyboard keys keep working beside them. |\n| `Controller` | `PrayerTab` | `DPadDown` | a button name | Controller button that switches the side panel between the inventory and the prayer book, as `[Interface] PrayerTabKey` does. |\n| `Controller` | `SpecFire` | `Y` | a button name | Controller button that fires the armed weapon's special attack, as `[Special] FireKey` does. |\n| `Controller` | `SpecSwitch` | `LeftStickButton` | a button name | Controller button that arms the next weapon you hold that has a special attack, as `[Special] SwitchKey` does. |\n| `Controller` | `CameraToggle` | `RightStickButton` | a button name | Controller button that switches the camera between near and far, as `[Camera] ToggleKey` does. |\n| `Controller` | `AttackStyle` | `Back` | a button name | Controller button that switches to your next attack style, as `[Interface] AttackStyleKey` does. |\n| `Dev` | `DumpData` | `false` | true / false | Writes Megabonk's loaded data (weapons, tomes, enemies, maps, characters, music) to `BepInEx/config/Bonkscape/dump.json`, and its controller setup (Rewired's actions and default gamepad map) to `input-dump.txt` beside it. For development. |\n| `Debug` | `HideMegabonkHud` | `true` | true / false | Hide Megabonk's own health bar, XP bar and monster health bars, which the OSRS HUD replaces. Off: the OSRS HUD is still drawn, Megabonk's bars stay up beside it, and Bonkscape doesn't read Megabonk's XP bar. For tracking down problems. |\n| `Debug` | `OsrsHud` | `true` | true / false | Draw Bonkscape's OSRS HUD. Off: no HUD is drawn, its interface sprites aren't loaded, and Megabonk's own HUD stays as it is. For tracking down problems. |\n| `Dev` | `AutoStartRun` | `false` | true / false | Starts a Lumbridge run with autoplay by itself, the way Melty's test does ([Testing](../dev/testing.md)). For development. |\n| `Dev` | `ManualTest` | `false` | true / false | Hand-over tests: Melty test runs leave the playing to you (no autoplay) while Bonkscape still writes its self-checks, for features autoplay can't reach ([Testing](../dev/testing.md)). |\n\nThe camera distance is applied at the start of every stage. The `Models` settings decide sizes when a run starts and\nwhen each monster spawns.\n\n## Other files\n\n`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Bonkscape\\settings.properties` is read if present: `OSRS_DIR=` (the OSRS folder Melty passes in) and\n`OSRS_CACHE=` (a cache folder, used when `OSRS.CacheFolder` is empty). Your saves and the log are listed in\n[Getting started](getting-started.md#where-your-progress-lives).\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Plugin.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Controls.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/CameraTweak.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Core/Sizing.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Dev/DataDump.cs -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "skilling", "text": "# Skilling\n\nEach map's own trees, rocks and shores are skilling spots (Lumbridge's, Ardougne & Seers' Village's, the God Wars Dungeon's, Al Kharid's, Morytania's, TzHaar City's, the Wilderness's). <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span>\n\n## How to gather\n\nStand next to a spot for **1.2 seconds**. Walking out of reach resets the timer. There's no button, no tool and no\nlevel requirement: being close is enough, so you can skill while you fight.\n\n| Spot | How many | Reach | Reward | XP | Back after |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Tree** (the map's trees and oaks) | 14 | about 1.8 tiles | **25 coins** and Megabonk's **Haste** speed boost. *\"You get some logs.\"* | 25 Woodcutting | 30 s |\n| **Rocks** | 10 | about 1.6 tiles | Megabonk's **Shield**. *\"You manage to mine some tin.\"* (the rock's ore) | 17.5 Mining | 30 s |\n| **Fishing spot** (on the water by the shore) | 6 | about 1.6 tiles | **Heals 20 HP**. *\"You catch some shrimps.\"* | 10 Fishing | 20 s |\n\nThe Haste and Shield are the same effects as Megabonk's own Haste and Shield pickups. Each spot plays an OSRS sound\nwhen you gather from it.\n\n## Where the spots are\n\n- **Trees and rocks** are the map's real OSRS objects: 14 of the objects named *Tree* or *Oak*, and 10 ore rocks (*Copper\n  rocks*, *Tin rocks*, *Iron rocks*, *Clay rocks*, *Coal rocks*; plain *Rocks* only when there are fewer than 4 ore\n  rocks). They're the same ones every run. The mining line names the rock's ore, *stone* for plain rocks.\n- **Fishing spots** are 6 water tiles next to walkable shore, in Lumbridge on the River Lum and in the swamp. Each shows OSRS's\n  fishing spot model on the water and disappears while it's used up.\n\nWithin 10 tiles of you, each usable spot shows its skill's icon, with a progress bar under it while you gather\n([HUD](hud-and-chat.md#in-a-run)). A used-up spot loses its icon; the tree or rock itself looks the same and gives\nnothing until it's back.\n\nIn the fallback stage ([Maps](maps.md#when-a-map-isnt-built)) the spots are OSRS models placed around where you\nstart: 10 trees, 8 rocks and 4 fishing spots.\n\n## The sheet and the code\n\nEach map row's skilling node names its reward, a row of the drops sheet's `skilling` table, and the reward is that\nrow's `effect` string:\n\n| Node | Drops row | Effect | What it does |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Tree | Logs | `gold:25;speed:0.2:6` | 25 coins, and Megabonk's Haste (its own strength and length, not the sheet's numbers) |\n| Rock | Copper ore | `armor:0.15:8` | Megabonk's Shield (likewise its own) |\n| Fishing | Raw shrimps | `heal:20` | Heals 20 |\n\nThe arena places 14/10/6 spots; the map row's counts (10/8/4) are used by the fallback stage, and\nthe respawn times by both.\n\nGathering levels don't change any reward yet.\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Skilling.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Hud.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Arena.cs sheets/maps.json sheets/drops.json sheets/skills.json -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "skills-and-xp", "text": "# Skills and XP\n\nBonkscape has ten OSRS skills. They're **kept between runs** and use OSRS's real 1-99 XP table.\n<span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> (XP drops and level-ups seen in Melty test runs).\n\n<!-- gen:skills -->\n| Skill | Trained by (sheet) | XP rate | Starting weapon unlocks | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Attack** | `melee_damage:accurate,controlled` | 0.25 | 1: Bronze scimitar / Iron scimitar, 5: Steel scimitar, 10: Black scimitar, 20: Mithril scimitar, 30: Adamant scimitar, 40: Rune scimitar, 42: Void knight mace, 60: Dragon scimitar / Dragon claws, 70: Abyssal whip, 75: Armadyl godsword, 80: Scythe of vitur | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Strength** | `melee_damage:aggressive,controlled` | 0.25 | 42: Void knight mace, 90: Scythe of vitur | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Defence** | `melee_damage:defensive,controlled; ranged_damage:longrange; magic_damage:defensive` | 0.25 | 42: Void knight mace | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Ranged** | `ranged_damage` | 0.25 | 1: Shortbow, 5: Oak shortbow, 20: Willow shortbow, 30: Maple shortbow, 40: Yew shortbow, 42: Void knight mace, 50: Magic shortbow, 55: Red chinchompa, 75: Toxic blowpipe | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Magic** | `magic_damage` | 0.25 | 1: Wind Strike, 5: Water Strike, 9: Earth Strike, 13: Fire Strike, 42: Void knight mace, 75: Trident of the seas, 94: Ice Barrage | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Hitpoints** | `any_damage:third` | 0.0833 | 42: Void knight mace | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Prayer** | `seconds_praying` | 2 | 22: Void knight mace | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Woodcutting** | `node:tree` | 25 | - | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Mining** | `node:rock` | 17.5 | - | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Fishing** | `node:fishing` | 10 | - | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n<!-- /gen:skills -->\n\n## The XP table\n\nThe same formula as OSRS: level *L* needs \u230a(1/4) \u00d7 \u03a3 from *l* = 1 to *L* \u2212 1 of \u230a*l* + 300 \u00d7 2^(*l*/7)\u230b\u230b XP.\n\n| Level | XP | Level | XP |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2 | 83 | 60 | 273,742 |\n| 10 | 1,154 | 70 | 737,627 |\n| 20 | 4,470 | 75 | 1,210,421 |\n| 30 | 13,363 | 80 | 1,986,068 |\n| 40 | 37,224 | 90 | 5,346,332 |\n| 50 | 101,333 | 99 | 13,034,431 |\n\nXP keeps counting past 99, up to 200,000,000 per skill. **Hitpoints starts at level 10** (1,154 XP), as in OSRS;\nevery other skill starts at 1.\n\n## What trains what\n\n**Combat skills** get XP for the damage you actually deal: the HP a monster loses, not the number Megabonk rolled.\n\nEach point of damage is worth 0.25 XP, split by the weapon's style and your [attack style](#attack-styles) as in\nOSRS, and Hitpoints gets a third of that (0.0833) on top:\n\n| Weapon | Attack style | Trains |\n|---|---|---|\n| Melee | Accurate | Attack |\n| Melee | Aggressive | Strength |\n| Melee | Controlled | Attack, Strength and Defence, a third each |\n| Melee | Defensive | Defence |\n| Ranged | Accurate or Rapid | Ranged |\n| Ranged | Longrange | Ranged and Defence, half each |\n| Magic | Casting | Magic |\n| Magic | Defensive casting | Magic (0.57) and Defence (0.43) |\n\nThe Pure never trains Defence: XP for it is dropped.\n\n## Attack styles\n\nEvery adventurer has one attack style, which decides only where its XP goes. It starts on its row's style (the\nWarrior, Zerker, Pure and Dharok aggressive, the Ironman and Torag defensive, the rest accurate) and is kept per\nadventurer. **F1** (`Interface.AttackStyleKey`, OSRS's own key for the combat tab; Back on a controller) moves to the next style and shows the\ncombat tab for 4 s; a click on a style on the combat tab picks it ([HUD](hud-and-chat.md#the-side-panel)). The chat box\nsays *\"Attack style: Longrange (Ranged, Defence XP).\"*\n\nThe styles follow your adventurer's own style: melee **Accurate**, **Aggressive**, **Controlled** and **Defensive**;\nranged **Accurate**, **Rapid** and **Longrange**; magic **Casting** and **Defensive casting**. A style that would\ntrain a skill the adventurer never trains isn't offered (the Pure has no Defensive or Controlled).\n\n**Prayer** gets 2 XP for every second a protection prayer is on. **Gathering skills** get a fixed amount per action:\nWoodcutting 25, Mining 17.5 and Fishing 10 ([Skilling](skilling.md)).\n\n## XP drops and level-ups\n\n- XP is grouped per OSRS game tick (0.6 s) and per skill. Each group is an OSRS **XP drop**, the skill icon and the\n  amount, rising into the **XP counter** beside the minimap, which shows your total XP over all skills\n  ([HUD](hud-and-chat.md#in-a-run)). Drops still waiting when a run ends are dropped; the XP is already yours.\n- On a level-up, the chat box says *\"Congratulations, you just advanced a Strength level. You are now level 41.\"* and\n  OSRS's level-up sound plays. OSRS's level-up dialogue then covers the chat box for 3 s (*\"Congratulations, you just\n  advanced a Strength level.\"*, *\"Your Strength level is now 41.\"*) and OSRS's level-up fireworks play at your feet.\n  (OSRS's level-up jingle is planned: the experimental music engine plays only the maps' tracks and the title\n  screen's Scape Main.)\n\n## Unlocks by level\n\nSkill levels decide your weapons, as OSRS's requirements do ([Weapons](weapons-and-evolutions.md#requirements)):\n\n- the **weapon ladders**: the Warrior, Ranger, Mage, Ironman and Pure start each run on the highest tier their own\n  levels allow (scimitars by Attack, shortbows by Ranged, the Strikes by Magic), and stronger weapons of their style\n  past the ladder's top ([Adventurers](adventurers.md#starting-weapons));\n- **level-up offers** leave out any weapon whose requirements you don't meet (one you hold or start with is always\n  offered).\n\nWhen a level brings a weapon into reach, the chat box says so: *\"You can now wield the rune scimitar (from your next\nrun).\"*, *\"You can now cast Fire Strike.\"*\n\nYour Prayer level also raises your prayer points (20 + level). The **Ironman** unlocks once any one adventurer you've played\n(one with a skills save of its own) reaches a **total level** (all its skill levels added up) of 250\n([Adventurers](adventurers.md#unlocking)). The\n**Pure** unlocks once one adventurer you've played has Attack 60 with Defence 1.\n\n## Combat level\n\nThe character select panel shows your **combat level**, worked out with OSRS's formula:\n\n- base = \u00bc \u00d7 (Defence + Hitpoints + \u230aPrayer / 2\u230b)\n- melee = 0.325 \u00d7 (Attack + Strength), ranged = 0.325 \u00d7 \u230a1.5 \u00d7 Ranged\u230b, magic = 0.325 \u00d7 \u230a1.5 \u00d7 Magic\u230b\n- combat level = \u230abase + the biggest of melee, ranged and magic\u230b\n\nA fresh save (10 Hitpoints, everything else 1) is combat level 3. Combat level doesn't affect play.\n\n## Saving\n\nEach adventurer keeps their own skills: **`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Bonkscape\\skills_<adventurer>.json`** (`skills_warrior.json`,\n`skills_zerker.json` and so on), a plain list of each skill's XP. An adventurer without a save yet starts from\nthe older shared `skills.json` if there is one (it is left as it was). A Barrows brother instead starts at level 70 in his\ncombat skills, and nothing is written for him until he earns XP. The character select panel shows the hovered\nadventurer's own levels and combat level. Bonkscape saves when anything changed, every 20 seconds, at the end of a run\nand when you quit Megabonk, writing a temporary file first so a crash never leaves half a save. If a file can't be\nread, that adventurer starts fresh (the log says *\"skills save of \u2026 unreadable, starting fresh\"*). To reset an\nadventurer's skills, delete their file while Megabonk is closed.\n\n<!-- sources: src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Skills.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Combat.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Content.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Prayer.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Skilling.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/CharacterSelect.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Hud.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/HudLayout.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/LevelUpFx.cs sheets/skills.json src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Unlocks.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/AttackStyles.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Core/Rows.cs src/Bonkscape.Plugin/Systems/Controls.cs -->\n"}, {"section": "wiki", "slug": "weapons-and-evolutions", "text": "# Weapons and evolutions\n\n## How a Bonkscape weapon works\n\nEvery OSRS weapon takes over one Megabonk weapon (its *Megabonk base*). It keeps that weapon's **behaviour**: how it\nattacks, its projectile and its visuals. Bonkscape replaces the rest:\n\n- **Base stats**: damage, cooldown, area, amount (projectiles), speed (projectile speed), bounces, duration and\n  knockback come from the row below.\n- **Level-up upgrades**: the weapon's Megabonk upgrade pool is replaced with the row's list.\n- **Name and icon**: the OSRS name, and an icon rendered from your cache. The four Strikes, Ice Barrage and the Fire\n  Surge evolution use their OSRS spell icons; the rest use the item's inventory icon.\n\nOn Bonkscape's maps, level-ups offer only Bonkscape's weapons: one for each of twelve Megabonk weapons (a ladder's\nat your tier), plus a Barrows brother's own weapon to him alone (Guthan's warspear, Torag's hammers and Verac's flail\nshare the Void knight mace's Megabonk weapon, so they replace the mace while their brother plays), and only those whose\n[requirements](#requirements) you meet. They all count as unlocked whatever your Megabonk progress is. When a weapon fires:\n\n- its projectile carries the OSRS model from the sheet, about a quarter of a tile along its longest side, centred\n  on the projectile and turned to point along its flight: each shortbow's arrow (iron for the\n  Shortbow up to rune for the yew and magic shortbows), the Toxic blowpipe's dragon dart, the Red chinchompa, Karil's crossbow's bolt, and the Strikes', Ice Barrage's, the Trident's and Ahrim's\n  staff's spell graphics (the Abyssal whip, Dragon scimitar, Scythe of vitur, Armadyl godsword, Dragon claws, Void\n  knight mace and the other Barrows weapons have none). Megabonk's own projectile effects stay;\n- the weapon's OSRS attack sound plays, at most every 0.3 s;\n- your adventurer takes that weapon in hand and plays its OSRS attack animation ([Adventurers](adventurers.md#looks)).\n\nHow the projectiles look in a run is *(unconfirmed: needs a Melty run or footage)*.\n\n## Weapon ladders\n\nThree of the weapons are **ladders** of OSRS tiers on one Megabonk weapon. The Warrior, Ranger, Mage, Ironman and Pure\nstart each run on the highest tier their own levels allow ([Adventurers](adventurers.md#starting-weapons)), and a\nlevel-up offers the ladder at your tier:\n\n| Ladder | Tiers, with the level each is climbed at |\n|---|---|\n| Scimitars (Attack) | Bronze 1, iron 2, steel 5, black 10, mithril 20, adamant 30, rune 40, dragon 60 |\n| Shortbows (Ranged) | Shortbow 1, oak 5, willow 20, maple 30, yew 40, magic 50 |\n| Strikes (Magic) | Wind 1, Water 5, Earth 9, Fire 13 |\n\nIron asks Attack 1 in OSRS, as bronze does, so a new adventurer starts with bronze and climbs to iron at Attack 2. Each\ntier has its own OSRS model and damage, from 0.70 of the top tier's at the bottom, and keeps its ladder's special\nattack (the scimitars' Sever, the shortbows' Snapshot; each Strike its own: Gale, Torrent, Quake and Wildfire). A tier\nreached during a run comes with the next one: *\"You can now wield the rune scimitar (from your next run).\"* The\nZerker keeps his own dragon scimitar whatever his Attack.\n\n## Requirements\n\nEvery weapon asks its OSRS levels: the ladders' tiers as above, the Abyssal whip Attack 70, the Armadyl godsword 75,\nDragon claws 60, the Scythe of vitur Attack 80 and Strength 90, the Toxic blowpipe Ranged 75, the Red chinchompa\nRanged 55, the Trident of the seas Magic 75, Ice Barrage Magic 94, the Void knight mace 42 in every combat skill and\nPrayer 22. A level-up never offers a weapon above your levels; one you hold already, start with or carry as an extra\nweapon (Durial321's Ice Barrage) is exempt. When a level brings one into reach, the chat box names it: *\"You can now\nwield the abyssal whip.\"*\n\n## Weapons\n\n<!-- gen:weapons -->\n| Weapon | OSRS item | Style | Megabonk base | Damage | Cooldown | Area | Amount | Speed | Bounces | Duration | Knockback | Skill levels to start a run with it | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Abyssal whip** | Abyssal whip | melee | Katana | 10 | 0.35 | 1.15 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0.5 | 1 | 70 Attack | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Dragon scimitar** | Dragon scimitar | melee | Sword | 11 | 0.7 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0.5 | 2 | 60 Attack | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Bronze scimitar** | Bronze scimitar | melee | Sword | 7.7 | 0.7 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0.5 | 2 | 1 Attack | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Iron scimitar** | Iron scimitar | melee | Sword | 7.9 | 0.7 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0.5 | 2 | 1 Attack | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Steel scimitar** | Steel scimitar | melee | Sword | 8.1 | 0.7 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0.5 | 2 | 5 Attack | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Black scimitar** | Black scimitar | melee | Sword | 8.2 | 0.7 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0.5 | 2 | 10 Attack | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Mithril scimitar** | Mithril scimitar | melee | Sword | 8.5 | 0.7 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0.5 | 2 | 20 Attack | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Adamant scimitar** | Adamant scimitar | melee | Sword | 8.9 | 0.7 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0.5 | 2 | 30 Attack | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Rune scimitar** | Rune scimitar | melee | Sword | 9.8 | 0.7 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0.5 | 2 | 40 Attack | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Magic shortbow** | Magic shortbow | ranged | Bow | 8 | 0.7 | 1 | 1 | 1.6 | 2 | 0.5 | 0.5 | 50 Ranged | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Shortbow** | Shortbow | ranged | Bow | 5.6 | 0.7 | 1 | 1 | 1.6 | 2 | 0.5 | 0.5 | 1 Ranged | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Oak shortbow** | Oak shortbow | ranged | Bow | 5.8 | 0.7 | 1 | 1 | 1.6 | 2 | 0.5 | 0.5 | 5 Ranged | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Willow shortbow** | Willow shortbow | ranged | Bow | 6.1 | 0.7 | 1 | 1 | 1.6 | 2 | 0.5 | 0.5 | 20 Ranged | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Maple shortbow** | Maple shortbow | ranged | Bow | 6.4 | 0.7 | 1 | 1 | 1.6 | 2 | 0.5 | 0.5 | 30 Ranged | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Yew shortbow** | Yew shortbow | ranged | Bow | 7.1 | 0.7 | 1 | 1 | 1.6 | 2 | 0.5 | 0.5 | 40 Ranged | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Toxic blowpipe** | Toxic blowpipe | ranged | Revolver | 4 | 1 | 1 | 6 | 2.2 | 0 | 1 | 0.4 | 75 Ranged | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Fire Strike** | Staff of fire | magic | FireStaff | 10 | 0.5 | 1 | 1 | 0.5 | 0 | 2 | 1 | 13 Magic | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Wind Strike** | Staff of air | magic | FireStaff | 7 | 0.5 | 1 | 1 | 0.5 | 0 | 2 | 1 | 1 Magic | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Water Strike** | Staff of water | magic | FireStaff | 8 | 0.5 | 1 | 1 | 0.5 | 0 | 2 | 1 | 5 Magic | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Earth Strike** | Staff of earth | magic | FireStaff | 9 | 0.5 | 1 | 1 | 0.5 | 0 | 2 | 1 | 9 Magic | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Ice Barrage** | Ancient staff | magic | Frostwalker | 9 | 1.25 | 1.1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1.6 | 0.5 | 94 Magic | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Trident of the seas** | Trident of the Seas | magic | LightningStaff | 8 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0.5 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 75 Magic | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Red chinchompa** | Red chinchompa | ranged | Rockets | 11 | 0.35 | 1.2 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 5 | 2 | 55 Ranged | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Dwarf multicannon** | Cannon base | ranged | new: deployable | 6 | 4 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 0 | 10 | 0.5 | 1 Ranged | <span class=\"st st-todo\">planned (phase 3)</span> |\n| **Dharok's greataxe** | Dharok's greataxe | melee | Axe | 14 | 1.6 | 1.3 | 1 | 0.5 | 0 | 0.82 | 2 | character:dharok | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Scythe of vitur** | Scythe of Vitur | melee | Scythe | 12 | 0.85 | 1.4 | 3 | 1 | 0 | 0.5 | 1 | 80 Attack, 90 Strength | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Armadyl godsword** | Armadyl godsword | melee | HeroSword | 16 | 1.2 | 1.3 | 1 | 30 | 0 | 0.5 | 3 | 75 Attack | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Dragon claws** | Dragon claws | melee | Dexecutioner | 9 | 0.6 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0.5 | 1 | 60 Attack | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Void knight mace** | Void knight mace | melee | CorruptSword | 10 | 0.85 | 1.1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0.5 | 2.5 | 42 Attack, 42 Strength, 42 Defence, 42 Hitpoints, 42 Ranged, 42 Magic, 22 Prayer | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Ahrim's staff** | Ahrim's staff | magic | BloodMagic | 10 | 1.1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0.75 | 1 | character:ahrim | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Guthan's warspear** | Guthan's warspear | melee | CorruptSword | 11 | 0.85 | 1.2 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0.5 | 1.5 | character:guthan | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Karil's crossbow** | Karil's crossbow | ranged | Sniper | 12 | 0.7 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 1 | 1 | 1 | character:karil | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Torag's hammers** | Torag's hammers | melee | CorruptSword | 12 | 0.85 | 1.1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0.5 | 2.5 | character:torag | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Verac's flail** | Verac's flail | melee | CorruptSword | 11 | 0.85 | 1.2 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0.5 | 2 | character:verac | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n<!-- /gen:weapons -->\n\n\"Skill levels to start a run with it\" only matters for the **starting** weapon\n([Adventurers](adventurers.md#starting-weapons)). Any weapon can turn up as a level-up offer.\n\nEach weapon trains a skill when it deals damage: melee weapons train Attack, Strength or Defence (by your\nadventurer's attack style), ranged weapons Ranged, magic weapons Magic, and all of them some Hitpoints\n([Skills and XP](skills-and-xp.md)).\n\n### Level-ups and special attacks\n\nWhen a weapon levels up, Megabonk offers upgrades from its pool. Bonkscape's pools:\n\n<!-- gen:weapon-levels -->\n| Weapon | Level-up upgrade pool | Special attack | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Abyssal whip** | damage +2.0 (flat); attack speed +0.08 (addition); attack size +0.15 (addition); crit chance +0.06 (flat) | Energy Drain (hit:1.25,slow:2:0.5:4) | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Dragon scimitar** | damage +2.0 (flat); attack size +0.2 (addition); projectiles +1 (flat); knockback +0.25 (addition) | Sever (hit:1.5,stun:1.5) | <span class=\"st st-verified\">verified</span> |\n| **Bronze scimitar** | damage +2.0 (flat); attack size +0.2 (addition); projectiles +1 (flat); knockback +0.25 (addition) | Sever (hit:1.5,stun:1.5) | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Iron scimitar** | damage +2.0 (flat); attack size +0.2 (addition); projectiles +1 (flat); knockback +0.25 (addition) | Sever (hit:1.5,stun:1.5) | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Steel scimitar** | damage +2.0 (flat); attack size +0.2 (addition); projectiles +1 (flat); knockback +0.25 (addition) | Sever (hit:1.5,stun:1.5) | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Black scimitar** | damage +2.0 (flat); attack size +0.2 (addition); projectiles +1 (flat); knockback +0.25 (addition) | Sever (hit:1.5,stun:1.5) | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Mithril scimitar** | damage +2.0 (flat); attack size +0.2 (addition); projectiles +1 (flat); knockback +0.25 (addition) | Sever (hit:1.5,stun:1.5) | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Adamant scimitar** | damage +2.0 (flat); attack size +0.2 (addition); projectiles +1 (flat); knockback +0.25 (addition) | Sever (hit:1.5,stun:1.5) | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Rune scimitar** | damage +2.0 (flat); attack size +0.2 (addition); projectiles +1 (flat); knockback +0.25 (addition) | Sever (hit:1.5,stun:1.5) | <span class=\"st st-built\">built</span> |\n| **Magic shortbow** | damage +1.6 (flat); projectiles +1 (flat); projectile speed +0.2 (addition); crit 